{"kind":"assert","text":"Current direction from hugh, 2026-10-03, recorded directly from his two messages in this planner session.\n\nSelf-host: development of artroom-jam can start when builder judges that Artroom, with declared acts, is complete enough to build it. Artroom will inevitably need further work arising, as well as existing backlog items. Builder owns the readiness judgment. Neither a separate hugh move decision nor completion of every platform/backlog/readiness item is a prerequisite for starting the jam.\n\nBuilding jam on its own acts model further allows that the workroom-style acts vocabulary may change while this self-hosting work is underway. Do not require a frozen platform-development verb list or force the jam to copy the present workroom vocabulary. Jam's application declarations can evolve for its own work. Workroom-style declarations may evolve from self-hosting evidence too; bind and activate changed meanings through the declared-acts model and retain their historical meanings for replay. Changes that require platform implementation remain tracked and reviewed under their own requests.\n\nThe former six-item self-host checklist is a set of useful concerns and follow-ups, not a universal completed start gate. The acts review is useful evidence and follow-up work, not a mandatory vocabulary freeze. Preserve existing acceptance and review obligations as work owed; readiness to start does not declare that work done. Record the builder's concrete capability judgment, remaining limits and first jam task in the workroom when reached. A later transfer of all platform development is tracked separately.\n\nThis is the current user direction, with a direct basis independent of the retired checklist. It consolidates and replaces the earlier planner formulation in e563b3f3.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","source":"hugh's two self-host clarifications in the current planner session, 2026-10-03"}}